{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. Classic Fibonacci-like. Count sequences of length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits. Let a_n be count. Recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2} + a_{n-3}? Wait for no 3 consecutive same. We can use DP with states: last run length and bit. Let's compute quickly.\n\nLet dp[n][k][b] where k=1 or 2 length of current run, b=0/1. For n=1: dp[1][1][0]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. For n>1: transition: if add same bit, only if k=1 -> new k=2; if k=2 cannot add same. If add opposite bit, new k=1.\n\nCompute iteratively.\n\nInitialize n=1: dp1: (k1,b0)=1, (k1,b1)=1.\n\nn=2: from each state:\n- from (1,0): add 0 -> (2,0)+=1; add 1 -> (1,1)+=1\n- from (1,1): add 1 -> (2,1)+=1; add 0 -> (1,0)+=1\nSo dp2: (2,0)=1, (1,1)=1, (2,1)=1, (1,0)=1.\n\nn=3: iterate:\nFrom (2,0): can only add 1 -> (1,1)+=1\nFrom (1,1): add 1 -> (2,1)+=1; add 0 -> (1,0)+=1\nFrom (2,1): add 0 -> (1,0)+=1\nFrom (1,0): add 0 -> (2,0)+=1; add 1 -> (1,1)+=1\n\nSum:\n(1,1): from (2,0)1 + from (1,0)1 =2\n(2,1): from (1,1)1 =1\n(1,0): from (1,1)1 + from (2,1)1 =2\n(2,0): from (1,0)1 =1\n\nn=4: compute:\nStates:\n(1,1)=2, (2,1)=1, (1,0)=2, (2,0)=1\n\nFrom (1,1): add1->(2,1)+=2; add0->(1,0)+=2\nFrom (2,1): add0->(1,0)+=1\nFrom (1,0): add0->(2,0)+=2; add1->(1,1)+=2\nFrom (2,0): add1->(1,1)+=1\n\nTotals:\n(2,1):2\n(1,0):2+1=3\n(2,0):2\n(1,1):2+1=3\n\nn=5:\nStates: (2,1)=2,(1,0)=3,(2,0)=2,(1,1)=3\n\nFrom (2,1): add0->(1,0)+=2\nFrom (1,0): add0->(2,0)+=3; add1->(1,1)+=3\nFrom (2,0): add1->(1,1)+=2"}}],"created":1790951214,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_de